    summary_en: "The European Commission is promoting the Cyber Resilience Act (CRA), which aims to ensure that all digital products placed on the EU market can withstand cyber threats. This law requires product security to cover its entire lifecycle, from design and updates to maintenance. The implementation of the Act involves cooperation among industry stakeholders, member states, and ENISA. According to the timeline, the EU is expected to release technical implementing rules for key products in November 2025, followed by the first set of Commission guidelines in early 2026. Key reporting obligations and standardization outcomes are expected to gradually take effect in the second half of 2026, with the Act fully applicable in December 2027. Manufacturers, SMEs, and open-source communities must pay attention to the relevant regulations, especially concerning the obligations for Conformity Assessment and the Single Reporting Platform.",
